DeathCoast contains code derived from Tablor (https://github.com/athousanddetails/schwung-tablor, commit
d51887187f7a03f7b32cc4a74f5c60c5532e65fa), vendored through https://github.com/saustin2010/mpc-vst-tablor.
Tablor itself is after Wavetable by Roland Rabien (FigBug) and uses AudioFilter (Michael Massberg), dr_flac
(David Reid) and pink noise code (Thomas Merchant, MIT). All are BSD-3-Clause / MIT / public domain; see LICENSE,
which is kept unchanged as the BSD-3-Clause terms require.

The wavetable library fetched at build time (release/library.json) is by Kristoffer Ekstrand (Adventure Kid,
public domain) and Neu KatalYst (free to use).

The history of changes is in CHANGES.md and PROJECT.md.
Neither the names of the copyright holders nor of the contributors are used to endorse DeathCoast.
